From 2200134cbcaf7e6b934eea28894eda4591a5609b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Schneiderman <JohnMS@member.fsf.org>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:23:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 45/69] Fix cast operand precedence for parenthesised
 expressions while preserving C++ expression parsing.

(cherry picked from commit 160c92b1ff614b3afa760c8d45bbfecf35984b2e)

Backport to v1.32.273 for nethack64.  The Parser change applies as is:
ParseCastExpression took a parenthesised operand without its postfix
operators, so `(int) (p)->f` and `(char *)(p)->f` cast p and then
applied ->f to the result ("Pointer expected").  It is nethack64's repro
r1 and the first compile error of ten NetHack files (obj_to_glyph,
get_artifact, EPRI).  The commit's two tests come with it; only their
registration in autotest.bat is merged by hand next to ours.
---
 autotest/autotest.bat        |  6 ++++
 autotest/castoperandtest.cpp | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 autotest/nestedviccasttest.c | 57 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 oscar64/Parser.cpp           |  7 +++--
 oscar64/Parser.h             |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 106 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 autotest/castoperandtest.cpp
 create mode 100644 autotest/nestedviccasttest.c

